@startuml
title Data definition and transfer - activity

start

:Project builds the workflow context\n(validated cfg, raw TOML);

:DataPlanner.build(config, domain_zone_ids,\nflow_active_bc, ...);
note right
  Explicit data.types win.
  Other types are inferred, each with a reason.
  In strict mode an inferred family needs
  its own data section.
end note
:Store the DataLoadPlan in the context;

:LoadDataStep runs run_data(config_path, data_plan, run_state);
:DataManagersRuntimeLoader.load_all(run_state);
:Fill loaded_data, one field per variable;

:apply_structural_updates_from_data();
if (geology loaded?) then (yes)
  :apply_geology_to_domain(domain, geology);
endif
if (oceanic loaded?) then (yes)
  :apply_oceanic_to_flow(flow, oceanic);
endif
if (recharge or ETP loaded?) then (yes)
  :apply_recharge_load_result_to_flow()\napply_etp_load_result_to_flow();
endif
:Bind lakes, barriers, cutoff walls\nand SFR networks to the flow;

:Continue with the simulation plan;
stop
@enduml
